3
00:00:04,933 --> 00:00:06,433
Let's find OUT!

4
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:09,400
Check this out,

5
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:11,200
a word analogy!

6
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,600
Hot is to cold,

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,000
as day is to...

8
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:16,600
what?

9
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:17,200
A.

10
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:17,800
Morning,

11
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:18,400
B.

12
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:19,000
Night,

13
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:19,600
C.

14
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:20,200
Sun,

15
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:21,400
or D.

16
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:22,000
Light?

17
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:23,200
Five seconds!

18
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,200
TIME'S UP!

19
00:00:30,867 --> 00:00:31,300
It's...

20
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:31,767
B,

21
00:00:31,767 --> 00:00:32,200
night!

22
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:34,400
Hot and cold are opposites,

23
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:37,067
so the opposite of day is

24
00:00:37,067 --> 00:00:37,500
night.

25
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:40,133
It is the same relationship, flipped.

26
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:41,933
Okay,

27
00:00:41,933 --> 00:00:43,833
