28
00:00:43,833 --> 00:00:44,467
Two,

29
00:00:44,467 --> 00:00:45,067
three,

30
00:00:45,067 --> 00:00:45,700
five,

31
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:46,333
eight,

32
00:00:46,333 --> 00:00:46,967
thirteen,

33
00:00:46,967 --> 00:00:48,233
and then...

34
00:00:48,233 --> 00:00:50,133
what comes next?

35
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:50,767
A.

36
00:00:50,767 --> 00:00:51,400
Eighteen,

37
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:52,033
B.

38
00:00:52,033 --> 00:00:52,633
Twenty,

39
00:00:52,633 --> 00:00:53,267
C.

40
00:00:53,267 --> 00:00:53,900
Twenty-one,

41
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:55,167
or D.

42
00:00:55,167 --> 00:00:55,800
Twenty-six?

43
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:57,067
Five seconds!

44
00:01:02,833 --> 00:01:04,033
TIME'S UP!

45
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:06,233
The answer is...

46
00:01:06,233 --> 00:01:06,733
C,

47
00:01:06,733 --> 00:01:07,267
twenty-one!

48
00:01:07,267 --> 00:01:10,300
Add the two numbers before it:

49
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:12,867
eight plus thirteen is twenty-one.

50
00:01:12,867 --> 00:01:15,433
It is the add-the-last-two pattern.

51
00:01:16,567 --> 00:01:17,700
Here's one,

52
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:19,400
